{
  "Study.Name": "Longitudinal Recovery Processes: 30-Day EMA Study",
  "authors": "Recovery Research Team",
  "funding": "National Institute on Drug Abuse (NIDA) Grant R01DA000000",
  "abstract": "This study investigates the dynamic processes of substance use recovery through 30 days of ecological momentary assessment (EMA). Participants complete a baseline demographic assessment followed by twice-daily surveys (morning and evening) assessing positive affect, negative affect, substance cravings, and perceived social support. The design aims to capture within-person fluctuations and between-person differences in recovery trajectories over a one-month period.",
